# Machine-local configuration for the pi web app, loaded by app.py via
# python-dotenv at startup — changes only take effect after a Flask
# restart (which also ends the chat session the running instance hosts).
#
# Not tracked by git (gitignored): every host keeps its own copy, so the
# settings below only apply to this machine. Real environment variables
# take precedence over the values here, which keeps one-off overrides on
# the command line working (VAR=... make run).
#
# This file is the only place documenting the available variables
# (see AGENTS.md): keep the commented-out entries up to date.

# Extra trusted Host headers, comma-separated; requests whose Host
# header matches none of the trusted names get a 400 Bad Request.
# Loopback, localhost, the hostname/FQDN, <hostname>.local and all local
# interface IPs are always trusted — list only names the server cannot
# discover itself, e.g. a systemd-nspawn container addressed by its
# machine name via nss-mymachines (resolvable only on the host).
# A leading dot matches all subdomains: .example.lan
#PI_WEB_TRUSTED_HOSTS=myhostname

# Bind address (default: the primary LAN IP, plus a permanent loopback
# listener). 127.0.0.1 restricts the server to loopback. 0.0.0.0 listens
# on ALL interfaces — dangerous: the server has no authentication and
# gives full agent access, so anyone on any reachable network (LAN,
# VPN, WiFi, possibly beyond) can drive it. Only use this on a fully
# trusted, isolated network — the default LAN-IP bind is the safer
# choice.
#HOST=127.0.0.1

# TCP port (default 5000).
#PORT=5000

# Confines projects and the file browser to this directory
# (default: the parent of the app dir).
#PI_WEB_WORKSPACE=/path/to/workspace
